-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/5 — בקשה לשיפוי עבור עובדי הוראה שזכאים להפרשי פיצויים עפ"י פסק הבוררות (פברואר 2009)
-- Chapter ה of the 14.4.2008 erosion award, quoted: teachers who left in
-- 2000–2007 on severance (not on pension) have it recomputed on a raised
-- determining salary. The owning bodies pay the differences and ask the
-- Ministry's indemnity committee for indemnity, one form per teacher, for
-- statutory severance (up to 100%) only.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `בקשה לשיפוי עבור עובדי הוראה שזכאים להפרשי פיצויים`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 The letterhead, title, date (February 2009), addressee, greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p11 The recital: further to the award of 14.4.2008 on erosion for teachers active in 2000–2007 (chapter ה) and to circular תשס"ח/8 §4, chapter ה is quoted; the quotation's rules are encoded below.

@desc A teacher who ended work with the employers, as chapter ה asks about them.
DECLARE `leaver` HAS
    `year the work ended`                  IS A NUMBER
    `left on pension`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid severance`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `years active in 2000-2002`            IS A NUMBER  @desc the length of the teacher's work in 2000–2002, in years (parts of a year as fractions)
    `years active in 2003-2006`            IS A NUMBER  @desc the length of the teacher's work in 2003–2006, in years (parts of a year as fractions)
    `statutory severance paid`             IS A NUMBER  @desc the severance paid under the law (up to 100%); an input
    `severance paid beyond the statute`    IS A NUMBER  @desc any severance paid beyond 100% of the statutory amount

-- ¶12–13: chapter ה covers teachers who ended their work with the
-- employers in the years examined (2000–2007, ¶11) other than by retiring
-- on pension: on severance pay.
@ref akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13
GIVEN l IS A `leaver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is covered by chapter ה` l IF
        l's `year the work ended` AT LEAST 2000
    AND l's `year the work ended` AT MOST 2007
    AND l's `paid severance`
    AND (NOT l's `left on pension`)

-- ¶14: those who ended their work in 2000–2006 have their severance
-- recomputed on a determining salary with these additions: those active in
-- 2000–2002 get part of the 4.75% addition, by the length of their work —
-- 1.8% a year.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN l IS A `leaver`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2000-2002 part by the rule` l IS
    min `the full 2000-2002 addition` (`the 2000-2002 addition a year` TIMES l's `years active in 2000-2002`)

`the full 2000-2002 addition` MEANS 4.75%
`the 2000-2002 addition a year` MEANS 1.8%

-- ¶15: those active in 2003–2006 get the addition "of 4.74%" and 0.8% for
-- each year, or the proportional part for part of a year, they were active
-- in 2003–2006. (The award names the base addition 4.75% in ¶14 and ¶23;
-- F-2008-09_tashsat_05-a. The base is a parameter so both can be tried.)
@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER, l IS A `leaver`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rule's addition on base` base l IS
    IF l's `years active in 2003-2006` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN base PLUS `the 2003-2006 addition a year` TIMES l's `years active in 2003-2006`
    ELSE `the 2000-2002 part by the rule` l

`the base addition as ¶15 prints it` MEANS 4.74%
`the 2003-2006 addition a year` MEANS 0.8%

-- ¶16–22, "the computation": the addition by the year the work ended.
-- ¶23: those who ended in 2007 are recomputed the same way but get 4% only,
-- the 4.75% being assumed already in their severance.
@ref akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p17 akn:hc_1/p18 akn:hc_1/p19 akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21 akn:hc_1/p22 akn:hc_1/p23
`the computation` MEANS
    LIST `ending-year row` 2000 (1.8%),
         `ending-year row` 2001 (3.6%),
         `ending-year row` 2002 (4.75%),
         `ending-year row` 2003 (5.55%),
         `ending-year row` 2004 (6.35%),
         `ending-year row` 2005 (7.15%),
         `ending-year row` 2006 (8.95%),
         `ending-year row` 2007 (4%)

@desc A row of the award's computation.
DECLARE `ending-year row` HAS
    `year ended`  IS A NUMBER
    `addition`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the computation's addition for` y IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `addition`)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `year ended` EQUALS y) `the computation`))

-- The reading adopted (F-2008-09_tashsat_05-a, -b): the computation's row
-- for the year the work ended governs, whatever part of that year was worked.
GIVEN l IS A `leaver`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the addition` l IS
    IF `is covered by chapter ה` l
    THEN `the computation's addition for` (l's `year the work ended`)
    ELSE 0

-- ¶24: the owning bodies are to locate everyone paid severance on ending
-- their work and pay the severance differences as above. No date is printed.
@ref akn:hc_1/p24
GIVEN l IS A `leaver`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `indemnity action`
DECIDE `the owning body locates and pays` l IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `locate the severance recipients`
    HENCE PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
          MUST  `pay the severance differences` x
                PROVIDED x AT LEAST `the indemnified differences` l

DECLARE `indemnity action` IS ONE OF
    `locate the severance recipients`
    `pay the severance differences` HAS `differences paid` IS A NUMBER
    `send an indemnity request on the form` HAS `request for` IS A `leaver`

-- ¶25, ¶27–28: to receive the indemnity, the owning body sends a request
-- for each teacher on the attached form, filled in carefully — for teachers
-- active in those years who retired and received severance only (not
-- through the pension funds) — to the coordinator of the indemnities
-- committee in the Ministry, Jerusalem.
@ref akn:hc_1/p25 akn:hc_1/p27 akn:hc_1/p28
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `indemnity action`
DECIDE `the owning body may ask for indemnity` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MAY   `send an indemnity request on the form` r
          PROVIDED `is covered by chapter ה` r

-- ¶26: it is severance under the law (up to 100%) and not beyond it.
-- Severance being proportional to the determining salary, the difference
-- is the statutory severance paid times the addition.
@ref akn:hc_1/p26
@export The severance differences the Ministry indemnifies an owning body for, for one teacher under chapter ה of the 14.4.2008 erosion award
GIVEN l IS A `leaver` @desc the teacher who left and the severance paid
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the indemnified differences` l IS
    l's `statutory severance paid` TIMES `the addition` l

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, signature and the link to download the form, which the corpus does not carry; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_05-a: the rule of ¶15, on the 4.75% the award names
-- elsewhere, gives 5.55%, 6.35% and 7.15% for those who worked through 2003,
-- 2004 and 2005 — the printed rows — and 7.95% for 2006, where the
-- computation prints 8.95%. On ¶15's own 4.74% no 2003–2006 row is matched.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `leaver`
DECIDE `a teacher active from 2000 to the end of` y IS
    `leaver` WITH
        `year the work ended`               IS y
        `left on pension`                   IS FALSE
        `paid severance`                    IS TRUE
        `years active in 2000-2002`         IS min 3 (y MINUS 1999)
        `years active in 2003-2006`         IS max 0 (min 4 (y MINUS 2002))
        `statutory severance paid`          IS 100000
        `severance paid beyond the statute` IS 0

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rule on 4.75% for a full final year` y IS
    `the rule's addition on base` `the full 2000-2002 addition` (`a teacher active from 2000 to the end of` y)

`2006's row is not the rule's` MEANS
        all (GIVEN y YIELD `the rule on 4.75% for a full final year` y EQUALS `the computation's addition for` y)
            (LIST 2000, 2001, 2002, 2003, 2004, 2005)
    AND `the rule on 4.75% for a full final year` 2006 EQUALS 7.95%
    AND NOT (`the computation's addition for` 2006 EQUALS 7.95%)
    AND all (GIVEN y YIELD NOT (`the rule's addition on base` `the base addition as ¶15 prints it` (`a teacher active from 2000 to the end of` y)
                                EQUALS `the computation's addition for` y))
            (LIST 2003, 2004, 2005, 2006)
#ASSERT `2006's row is not the rule's`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_05-b: a teacher who left in March 2004 has 1 2/12
-- years in 2003–2006; the rule gives 4.75% + 0.8% × 14/12, the computation
-- 6.35%.
`left in March 2004` MEANS
    `leaver` WITH
        `year the work ended`               IS 2004
        `left on pension`                   IS FALSE
        `paid severance`                    IS TRUE
        `years active in 2000-2002`         IS 3
        `years active in 2003-2006`         IS 14/12
        `statutory severance paid`          IS 100000
        `severance paid beyond the statute` IS 0

`the rule pro-rates a part year and the computation does not` MEANS
    NOT (`the rule's addition on base` `the full 2000-2002 addition` `left in March 2004`
         EQUALS `the computation's addition for` 2004)
#ASSERT `the rule pro-rates a part year and the computation does not`

-- Examples. Severance of 100,000 is a placeholder.
#ASSERT `the indemnified differences` `left in March 2004` EQUALS 6350
#ASSERT `the indemnified differences` (`a teacher active from 2000 to the end of` 2007) EQUALS 4000

#TRACE `the owning body locates and pays` `left in March 2004` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `locate the severance recipients` AT 1
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the severance differences` 6350 AT 2
#TRACE `the owning body may ask for indemnity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send an indemnity request on the form` `left in March 2004` AT 3
